# SRG-APP-001035-WSR-000340  -  CAT I
# The web server must be a version supported by the vendor.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-001035-WSR-000340
group:           V-279029
severity:        high
cat:             CAT I
determination:   ORGANIZATIONAL
grade:           C
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-003376
control_rev5:    SA-22

contribution:    The HTTP service in scope is the Splunk Web application server bundled
                 inside Splunk Enterprise and started by web.conf [settings] startwebserver
                 (web.conf.spec:23), not a separately procured and separately versioned web
                 server product, so the application's contribution is to serve that
                 component from the single installed Splunk Enterprise release and report
                 that release through its own interfaces; the specification set exposes no
                 version or support attribute for the embedded server, and no setting that
                 makes its release a supported one.

external:        Software deployment that fixes the installed release: Splunk Web is
                 patched by rebuilding or reinstalling the Splunk Enterprise package or
                 image, and there is no separate web server package to update.
external:        Splunk Enterprise software maintenance and support entitlement covering
                 the installed release, which carries Splunk Web.
external:        Organizational software lifecycle and patch management procedure
                 establishing the supported-release baseline and the upgrade trigger before
                 vendor end of support.
external:        Where the organization places a separately procured HTTP front end in the
                 boundary, that product is a distinct component assessed for version
                 support under its own baseline and entitlement, not against the Splunk
                 application.

manual_reason:   Splunk Web has no release or support attribute of its own: its support
                 status is the support status of the Splunk Enterprise release that carries
                 it, which is a property of the installed package rather than of
                 configuration. checks.tsv assigns no conf, stanza, or key to this
                 requirement, and the sweep of all 67 Splunk 10.4.2 *.conf.spec files
                 returns no key reporting or constraining an embedded HTTP server version
                 or support level; the only version-adjacent web setting is
                 web.conf.spec:192-196 updateCheckerBaseURL, a release-notification URL
                 that may be disabled, which does not determine support status. Deciding
                 this requirement requires reading the installed release, which is not
                 Splunk configuration, so no condition in the criterion vocabulary can be
                 written over it.

citation:        Web Server SRG V4R5, SRG-APP-001035-WSR-000340 (V-279029), severity high,
                 CCI-003376, SA-22 a: check text "Verify that the web server is a version
                 supported by the vendor"; fix text "Install or upgrade the webserver to a
                 version supported by the vendor." No product STIG rule shares CCI-003376;
                 the sunset Splunk Enterprise 8.x for Linux STIG V2R3 SPLK-CL-000510
                 (V-274465) fix text is "Upgrade to a version supported by the vendor.",
                 naming no configuration value. Specification basis that the web server is
                 an internal component of the product rather than a separately versioned
                 one: web.conf.spec:16 [settings], web.conf.spec:23 startwebserver,
                 web.conf.spec:28 httpport, web.conf.spec:70 enableSplunkWebSSL; only
                 version-adjacent web setting: web.conf.spec:192-196 updateCheckerBaseURL.
finding:         This determination is made from the perspective of the application layer
                 alone: the web server addressed here is the Splunk Web component of Splunk
                 Enterprise, which exposes no configuration setting bearing on its own
                 version support, so the application's share of this requirement is limited
                 to serving that component from, and reporting, the single installed Splunk
                 Enterprise release, and a finding is sustained only where that release is
                 at or past the vendor's published end of support, or where a separately
                 procured HTTP front end in the boundary runs an unsupported version under
                 its own baseline, in either case remedied by upgrading the product rather
                 than by any Splunk configuration change.
